# designs/ovodyo/ci.cog — assembled standing-frame CoG / tip-over check
# (tools/cogcheck, scripts/cog-check.sh, issue #623; product half of #603 item 10).
#
# Opt-in by presence. TIP-RISK is an advisory WARN, never a hard fail — do not
# "fix" geometry to force STABLE. A broken line or an STL the gate did not
# render IS a hard fail.
#
# Units: density g/cm³, mass g, length mm. rotate then translate (OpenSCAD:
# rotate([x,y,z]) = Rz·Ry·Rx). Printed PLA density is the repo convention 1.24
# applied to the SOLID mesh volume — the slicer infill (15–20 %) is invisible
# here, so the balls are OVER-massed vs a real print (conservative toward
# TIP-RISK). Non-printed hardware is mass: point masses. mock-drive and
# seam-coupon are gated printability samples, not standing-assembly parts.
#
# Part basenames are gate.sh's build/<design>-<ci.parts value>.stl — never a
# bare hours-top.stl, never a path. Duplicate STL basenames are forbidden:
# ci.parts lists base-end and base-plug once (print two in the slicer); the
# second copy is a mass: at the mirrored / other-port pose, not a second part:.
#
# Defaults cited from designs/ovodyo/ovodyo.scad unless noted:
#   ball_d=78, ball_spacing=200, ball_center_z=124, stalk_d=4.5,
#   truss_h=34, seg_len=127, core_len=120, core_h=8.8, core_wall=1.4,
#   core_port_wall=4.2, plug_head_h=1.2, _port_z=5.75.
# Ballast fill: NOTES.md "Ballast (stated assumption)" ≈55 g (2×28 g) Ø2 mm
# steel shot — a starting fill to tune against the measured verdict, not a
# STABLE claim.

margin: 2.0

# ---- ball halves (print: pole-down, seam on the bed; module ball_half) ------
# Print frame: translate([0,0,R]) of the seated hemisphere (R = ball_d/2 = 39);
# the top half also rotate([180,0,0]) so its outer pole is on the bed.
# Seated frame has the ball centre at the origin and the equator at z=0.
# Standing: hours centre (-100,0,124), minutes (100,0,124).
# Bottom STL centre is at (0,0,R) → translate (±100, 0, 124-R) = (±100,0,85).
# Top STL: undoing the print Rx(180) with rotate: 180,0,0 then translating the
# print-frame origin (the outer pole) to (±100, 0, 124+R) = (±100,0,163)
# puts the centre at z=124 (Rx(180) of (0,0,R) is (0,0,-R); +163 → 124).
part: ovodyo-hours-top.stl     | density: 1.24 | translate: -100,0,163 | rotate: 180,0,0
part: ovodyo-hours-bottom.stl  | density: 1.24 | translate: -100,0,85
part: ovodyo-minutes-top.stl   | density: 1.24 | translate:  100,0,163 | rotate: 180,0,0
part: ovodyo-minutes-bottom.stl| density: 1.24 | translate:  100,0,85

# ---- base, modelled in the standing frame already (z=0 deck) ---------------
# base-end is the −x wing (stations 0..bays, stalk at x=−100) as base_end().
# base-segment / base-core sit on the deck as exported. base-plug prints
# head-down at the origin; core_plug_seated(+1) is
# translate([core_len/2 + plug_head_h, +_port_y, _port_z]) rotate([0,-90,0])
# = translate(61.2, 22, 5.75) rotate(0,-90,0). The −y port is a mass: below.
part: ovodyo-base-segment.stl  | density: 1.24
part: ovodyo-base-end.stl      | density: 1.24
part: ovodyo-base-core.stl     | density: 1.24
part: ovodyo-base-plug.stl     | density: 1.24 | translate: 61.2,22,5.75 | rotate: 0,-90,0

# ---- brass stalks (vitamin Ø4.5 rod, brass ~8.5 g/cm³) ---------------------
# Length L = ball_center_z − base_h(±100). |x|=100 is on an end wing:
# base_t(100) = 1 − (100 − seg_len/2)/seg_len = 1 − 36.5/127 = 0.712598…
# base_h = truss_h·t = 24.228 mm; L = 99.772 mm.
# V = π·(d/2)²·L = 1.5868 cm³ → 13.49 g. Cylinder centroid at
# z = base_h + L/2 = 74.11 mm, x = ±100 (module stalk()).
mass: stalk-hours   | grams: 13.49 | at: -100,0,74.11
mass: stalk-minutes | grams: 13.49 | at:  100,0,74.11

# ---- steel shot ballast (NOTES: ≈55 g total, starting fill) ----------------
# Two pockets, s=±1, from _pocket_sec / _core_pocket. Uniform-section
# centroid of the y–z polygon (socket-hump subtraction ignored — it removes
# a little fill next to the deck struts): y_abs = 21.65 mm, z = 3.91 mm.
# Along x the pocket runs [−core_len/2 + core_wall, +core_len/2 − core_port_wall]
# = [−58.6, 55.8], midpoint x = −1.4 mm (thicker +x port wall). NOTES rounds
# this to "z ≈ 5 mm"; 27.5 g each so the two masses sum to the 55 g starting
# fill rather than 2×28 = 56. Tune the fill against the gate's verdict —
# do not read STABLE into this number.
mass: ballast-neg | grams: 27.5 | at: -1.4,-21.65,3.91
mass: ballast-pos | grams: 27.5 | at: -1.4, 21.65,3.91

# ---- second printed copies (not a second part: line) -----------------------
# +x wing: full_base() mirrors the −x wing in x. PLA estimate from the
# inline strut/boss/foot/nose inventory of base_end() (cylinder lengths of
# strut_d=2.8, node-sphere overlaps ignored): V ≈ 7.16 cm³ → 8.9 g at
# strut-midpoint CoG (−110.9, −0.1, 6.5); mirrored x → (110.9, −0.1, 6.5).
# Replace grams with mesh volume × 1.24 of ovodyo-base-end.stl once a gate
# render measures it.
mass: base-end-plus | grams: 8.9 | at: 110.9,-0.1,6.5
# −y ballast plug: same PLA frustum-head estimate as core_plug()
# (head Ø5×1.2 + taper 3.3→2.7 × 4.5 mm → 0.069 g). Print-frame CoG ≈
# (0,0,2.15); after rotate([0,-90,0]) + translate(61.2, −22, 5.75) →
# (63.35, −22, 5.75). Geared steppers / PCB omitted — NOTES gives no mass.
mass: base-plug-neg | grams: 0.069 | at: 63.35,-22,5.75
